From b465af33763eb48425042080ff6b71aa61c1ff83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-v9 <v9@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 22:22:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] v9: keep short-circuit || diamonds branchy in
 if-conversion

 (a || b) if-converts to a cmov chain, but its whole point is
short-circuit evaluation: a branch is cheaper and lets the backend fuse each
compare straight into a jump (no setcc+movzbl+test+cmov per link). Skip
if-conversion when every converted phi has the || shape (true arm == const 1)
and its result is consumed only by control flow (branch conditions, boolean
negations Cmp(Eq/Ne,0/1), Select conditions, through Copy/Cast/Phi edges).

The && shape (false arm == const 0) is still converted, because that is the
Select(cond, Cmp, 0) pattern the range-check fold collapses into one sub+cmp,
which then fuses into the surrounding || branch.

Measured: expat_xml_scan 3.13x -> 2.90x; regression 127 passed / 0 failed,
correctness 50/50, intrinsics 3/3. New unit tests test_value_only_controls_branch
and test_skip_boolean_diamond_or_shape.
---
 src/passes/if_convert.rs | 297 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 296 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

