From f5a349342fafbf6cac47510fdd346a5914ec41fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-v9 <v9@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 22:22:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] v9: fuse Cmp->Cast->branch flag chains (extend the
 pending-flag handshake)

The fused Cmp chain walk (prologue.rs) previously allowed only flag-neutral
Copy instructions between a Cmp and its Select/CondBranch consumer. Extend it
to integer Casts (mov/movzx/movsx leave the flags intact), so the range-check
fold's Cmp -> Cast(bool, I8->I64) -> CondBranch fuses into a single cmp;jcc
instead of setcc+movzbl+test. The Cast destination must still have exactly
one use (only the next chain link or the consumer), preserving the existing
soundness rule that every fused value is read exactly once.

Measured with the || skip: expat's first range check now emits
'sub /bin/bashx61; cmp /bin/bashx19; ja' with no boolean materialization.
